#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:138
msgid ""
"This library provides 4 functions: `js2xml()`, `json2xml()`, `xml2js()`, "
"and `xml2json()`. Here are the usages for each one (see more details in "
"the following sections):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:147
msgid "Convert JS object / JSON → XML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:149
msgid ""
"To convert JavaScript object to XML text, use `js2xml()`. To convert JSON"
" text to XML text, use `json2xml()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:159
msgid "Options for Converting JS object / JSON → XML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:161
msgid ""
"The below options are applicable for both `js2xml()` and `json2xml()` "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "Option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`spaces`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Number of spaces to be used for indenting XML output. Passing characters "
"like `' '` or `'\\t'` are also accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`compact`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether the *input* object is in compact form or not. By default, input "
"is expected to be in non-compact form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"IMPORTANT: Remeber to set this option `compact: true` if you are "
"supplying normal json (which is likely equivalent to compact form). "
"Otherwise, the function assumes your json input is non-compact form and "
"you will not get a result if it is not in that form. See "
"[Synopsis](#synopsis) to know the difference between the two json forms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`fullTagEmptyElement`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to produce element without sub-elements as full tag pairs "
"`<a></a>` rather than self closing tag `<a/>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`indentCdata`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to write CData in a new line and indent it. Will generate `<a>\\n"
" <![CDATA[foo]]></a>` instead of `<a><![CDATA[foo]]></a>`. See "
"[discussion](https://github.com/nashwaan/xml-js/issues/14)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`indentAttributes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to print attributes across multiple lines and indent them (when "
"`spaces` is not `0`). See [example](https://github.com/nashwaan/xml-"
"js/issues/31)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`ignoreDeclaration`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore writing declaration directives of xml. For example, "
"`<?xml?>` will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`ignoreInstruction`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore writing processing instruction of xml. For example, "
"`<?go there?>` will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`ignoreAttributes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore writing attributes of the elements. For example, "
"`x=\"1\"` in `<a x=\"1\"></a>` will be ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`ignoreComment`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore writing comments of the elements. That is, no `<!--  "
"-->` will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`ignoreCdata`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore writing CData of the elements. That is, no `<![CDATA[ "
"]]>` will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`ignoreDoctype`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore writing Doctype of the elements. That is, no `<!DOCTYPE"
" >` will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`ignoreText`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore writing texts of the elements. For example, `hi` text "
"in `<a>hi</a>` will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:180
msgid "Convert XML → JS object / JSON"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:182
msgid ""
"To convert XML text to JavaScript object, use `xml2js()`. To convert XML "
"text to JSON text, use `xml2json()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:192
msgid "Options for Converting XML → JS object / JSON"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:194
msgid ""
"The below options are applicable for both `xml2js()` and `xml2json()` "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "Whether to produce detailed object or compact object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`trim`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to trim whitespace characters that may exist before and after the"
" text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`sanitize` ([Deprecated](https://github.com/nashwaan/xml-js/issues/26))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to replace `&` `<` `>` with `&amp;` `&lt;` `&gt;` respectively, "
"in the resultant text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`nativeType`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to attempt converting text of numerals or of boolean values to "
"native type. For example, `\"123\"` will be `123` and `\"true\"` will be "
"`true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`nativeTypeAttributes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to attempt converting attributes of numerals or of boolean values"
" to native type. See also `nativeType` above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`addParent`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to add `parent` property in each element object that points to "
"parent object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`alwaysArray`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Whether to always put sub element, even if it is one only, as an item "
"inside an array. `<a><b/></a>` will be `a:[{b:[{}]}]` rather than "
"`a:{b:{}}` (applicable for compact output only). If the passed value is "
"an array, only elements with names in the passed array are always made "
"arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`alwaysChildren`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Whether to always generate `elements` property even when there are no "
"actual sub elements. `<a></a>` will be "
"`{\"elements\":[{\"type\":\"element\",\"name\":\"a\",\"elements\":[]}]}` "
"rather than `{\"elements\":[{\"type\":\"element\",\"name\":\"a\"}]}` "
"(applicable for non-compact output)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`instructionHasAttributes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Whether to parse contents of Processing Instruction as attributes or not."
" `<?go to=\"there\"?>` will be "
"`{\"_instruction\":{\"go\":{\"_attributes\":{\"to\":\"there\"}}}}` rather"
" than `{\"_instruction\":{\"go\":\"to=\\\"there\\\"\"}}`. See "
"[discussion](https://github.com/nashwaan/xml-js/issues/17)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore parsing declaration property. That is, no `declaration`"
" property will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore parsing processing instruction property. That is, no "
"`instruction` property will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore parsing attributes of elements.That is, no `attributes`"
" property will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore parsing comments of the elements. That is, no `comment`"
" will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore parsing CData of the elements. That is, no `cdata` will"
" be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore parsing Doctype of the elements. That is, no `doctype` "
"will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore parsing texts of the elements. That is, no `text` will "
"be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:215
msgid "The below option is applicable only for `xml2json()` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"Number of spaces to be used for indenting JSON output. Passing characters"
" like `' '` or `'\\t'` are also accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:221
msgid "Options for Changing Key Names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:223
msgid ""
"To change default key names in the output object or the default key names"
" assumed in the input JavaScript object / JSON, use the following "
"options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`declarationKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"declaration\"` or `\"_declaration\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the declaration. For "
"example, if `declarationKey: '$declaration'` then output of `<?xml?>` "
"will be `{\"$declaration\":{}}` *(in compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`instructionKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"instruction\"` or `\"_instruction\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the processing "
"instruction. For example, if `instructionKey: '$instruction'` then output"
" of `<?go there?>` will be `{\"$instruction\":{\"go\":\"there\"}}` *(in "
"compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`attributesKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"attributes\"` or `\"_attributes\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the attributes. For "
"example, if `attributesKey: '$attributes'` then output of `<a "
"x=\"hello\"/>` will be `{\"a\":{$attributes:{\"x\":\"hello\"}}}` *(in "
"compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`textKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"text\"` or `\"_text\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the text. For example, if"
" `textKey: '$text'` then output of `<a>hi</a>` will be "
"`{\"a\":{\"$text\":\"Hi\"}}` *(in compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`cdataKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"cdata\"` or `\"_cdata\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the cdata. For example, "
"if `cdataKey: '$cdata'` then output of `<![CDATA[1 is < 2]]>` will be "
"`{\"$cdata\":\"1 is < 2\"}` *(in compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`doctypeKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"doctype\"` or `\"_doctype\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the doctype. For example,"
" if `doctypeKey: '$doctype'` then output of `<!DOCTYPE foo>` will be "
"`{\"$doctype\":\" foo}` *(in compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`commentKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"comment\"` or `\"_comment\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the comment. For example,"
" if `commentKey: '$comment'` then output of `<!--note-->` will be "
"`{\"$comment\":\"note\"}` *(in compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`parentKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"parent\"` or `\"_parent\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the parent. For example, "
"if `parentKey: '$parent'` then output of `<a></b></a>` will be "
"`{\"a\":{\"b\":{$parent:_points_to_a}}}` *(in compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`typeKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"type\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the type. For example, if"
" `typeKey: '$type'` then output of `<a></a>` will be "
"`{\"elements\":[{\"$type\":\"element\",\"name\":\"a\"}]}` *(in non-"
"compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`nameKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"name\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the name. For example, if"
" `nameKey: '$name'` then output of `<a></a>` will be "
"`{\"elements\":[{\"type\":\"element\",\"$name\":\"a\"}]}` *(in non-"
"compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`elementsKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`\"elements\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Name of the property key which will be used for the elements. For "
"example, if `elementsKey: '$elements'` then output of `<a></a>` will be "
"`{\"$elements\":[{\"type\":\"element\",\"name\":\"a\"}]}` *(in non-"
"compact form)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:239
msgid ""
"Two default values mean the first is used for *non-compact* output and "
"the second is for *compact* output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:241
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**TIP**: In compact mode, you can further reduce output result by using "
"fewer characters for key names `{textKey: '_', attributesKey: '$', "
"commentKey: 'value'}`. This is also applicable to non-compact mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:243
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**TIP**: In non-compact mode, you probably want to set `{textKey: "
"'value', cdataKey: 'value', commentKey: 'value'}`  to make it more "
"consistent and easier for your client code to go through the contents of "
"text, cdata, and comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:246
msgid "Options for Custom Processing Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:248
msgid ""
"For XML → JS object / JSON, following custom callback functions can be "
"supplied:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "Signature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`doctypeFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`(value, parentElement)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for DOCTYPE. For example, `{doctypeFn: "
"function(val) {return val.toUpperCase();}}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`instructionFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`(instructionValue, instructionName, parentElement)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for content of Processing Instruction "
"value. For example, `{instructionFn: function(val) {return "
"val.toUpperCase();}}`. Note: `instructionValue` will be an object if "
"`instructionHasAttributes` is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`cdataFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for CData. For example, `{cdataFn: "
"function(val) {return val.toUpperCase();}}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`commentFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for comments. For example, `{commentFn: "
"function(val) {return val.toUpperCase();}}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`textFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for texts inside elements. For example, "
"`{textFn: function(val) {return val.toUpperCase();}}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`instructionNameFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`(instructionName, instructionValue, parentElement)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for Processing Instruction name. For "
"example, `{instructionNameFn: function(val) {return "
"val.toUpperCase();}}`. Note: `instructionValue` will be an object if "
"`instructionHasAttributes` is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`elementNameFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for element name. For example, "
"`{elementNameFn: function(val) {return val.toUpperCase();}}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`attributeNameFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`(attributeName, attributeValue, parentElement)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for attribute name. For example, "
"`{attributeNameFn: function(val) {return val.toUpperCase();}}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`attributeValueFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`(attributeValue, attributeName, parentElement)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for attributeValue. For example, "
"`{attributeValueFn: function(val) {return val.toUpperCase();}}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`attributesFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for attributes object. For example, "
"`{attributesFn: function(val) {return val.toUpperCase();}}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md:271
msgid ""
"For JS object / JSON → XML, following custom callback functions can be "
"supplied:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`(value, currentElementName, currentElementObj)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"To perform additional processing for DOCTYPE. For example, `{doctypeFn: "
"function(val) {return val.toUpperCase();}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"`(instructionValue, instructionName, currentElementName, "
"currentElementObj)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid ""
"`(instructionName, instructionValue, currentElementName, "
"currentElementObj)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`(attributeName, attributeValue, currentElementName, currentElementObj)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`(attributeValue, attributeName, currentElementName, currentElementObj)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`fullTagEmptyElementFn`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
msgid "`(currentElementName, currentElementObj)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/xml-js_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Whether to generate full tag or just self closing tag for elements that "
"has no sub elements. For example, `{fullTagEmptyElementFn: function(val) "
"{return val === 'foo'}}`."
msgstr ""

